<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36399" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pīrātĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειρατικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			pirates</i>, <i>piratic</i>, <i>piratical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myoparone piratico capto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 28, § 73</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 26, 30, § 152</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurea,</span>”
				<i>victories over the pirates</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 122</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Red. in Sen. 5, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pīrātĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>piracy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piraticam queque ut musicam fabricam dici adhuc
					dubitabant mei praeceptores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 34</span></i>
			:  piraticam facere, <i>to practise
				piracy</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Red. in Sen. 5</span></i>; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piraticam exercere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					8, 3, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">22, 1,
		14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
